Spec: Admin Frontend

Purpose:
  Native C++/Qt UI for managing and monitoring the MitM Data Aggregator.

Platform: C++

References:
  ../mitm-2.sdd

Owns:
  ./**

Depends on:
  /admin/dashboard/stats

Must:
  Display DB information and DLQ cursor count on the dashboard (Issue #4).
  Avoid using hardcoded fallback authentication tokens.
  Manage object lifecycles safely to avoid use-after-free conditions.
  Sanitize all OS inputs, such as environment variables, before using them in file paths.
  Reduce the lifetime of secrets in memory and implement secure wiping for password/proxy buffers.
  Avoid passing proxy credentials as URL strings in plain text and prohibit dummy credentials.
  Handle API error responses, timeouts, and HTTP status codes (e.g., 401/403) uniformly via a central API client.
  Pin third-party dependencies (e.g., QXlsx) to verified release tags or commit hashes.
  Secure dependencies using lockfiles (SBOM) and regular vulnerability scanning.
  Establish CTest and CI pipelines for testing configuration, cryptography, and UI logic.

Tasks:
  [x] #4 Introduce a common API client module to uniformly handle HTTP status codes, schemas, timeouts, and error responses.
  [x] #5 Implement secure memory wiping (e.g., sodium_memzero) for password and proxy buffers to reduce secret lifetime.
  [x] #6 Refactor proxy credential handling to avoid plain text URL strings and reject unauthenticated dummy credentials.
  [x] #7 Validate user roles before sensitive UI actions and prompt for re-authentication on 401/403 responses.
  [x] #8 Pin the QXlsx dependency in CMake to a verified release tag or commit hash instead of tracking the master branch.
  [x] #9 Setup CTest and Continuous Integration (CI) pipelines for core components (crypto, config, roles).
  [x] #10 Introduce dependency lockfiles (SBOM) and regular vulnerability scanning.
  [x] #11 Add telemetry for network latencies, API error rates, and update checks.
  [x] #12 Consolidate secret management to align with the overall MitM Scheduler strategy. (Skipped per user request - maintaining current implementation)
  [x] #13 Update the C++ standard in CMakeLists.txt to C++26.
  [x] #14 Increase cmake_minimum_required in CMakeLists.txt to at least 3.25.
  [x] #15 Run a local CMake configure and build step to verify compiler compatibility.
  [x] #16 Migrate the remaining 6 widgets to the new ApiClient.
  [x] #17 Fix semantic version comparison in update checker so older versions aren't flagged as updates.
  [x] #18 Feature: Issue #4 - Fetch and display dashboard stats from /admin/dashboard/stats
  [x] #2 Make Job-Log export report filename and date selection more user-friendly.
  [x] #3 Add optional time range filter (from/to) for Job-Audit-Log listing.
  [x] Github Issue #5: Extending menu "Info->About" dialog to link to latest release.
  [x] Github Issue #6: Fix empty export report by fetching full API data for the chosen date range instead of relying on the filtered model.
  [x] Github Issue #7: Desktop-UI clean-up, move settings tabs under a new "System / Settings" tab.
  [x] Github Issue #6: Feature: Implement Settings Key Vault (Store MASTER_KEY securely in memory, add lock/unlock UI)
